%% D33 Incident Command lifecycle
%% Type: state · Page: /architecture/operations, /enterprise/operations
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> CLARIFY: impact · severity · commander named
  CLARIFY --> CONTAIN: containment actions declared (pause dispatch · quarantine · hold publication)
  CONTAIN --> OBSERVE: every action has COMMAND · ACK · EFFECT_OBSERVED
  OBSERVE --> ISOLATE: forensic bundle preserved
  ISOLATE --> RESTORE: failed layer identified (intent · context · model · tool · state · policy · evaluation)
  RESTORE --> CORRECT: incident-scoped restoration Decision + known-safe evidence
  CORRECT --> PREVENT: defect corrected
  PREVENT --> MEASURE: regression case + control added (Improvement Candidate)
  MEASURE --> RESOLVED: fix holds over window · unknowns dispositioned
  RESOLVED --> [*]
  note right of CONTAIN
    Acknowledgment ≠ containment.
    Only the independent observer records EFFECT_OBSERVED.
  end note
  note right of RESTORE
    Restoration is a new consequential action
    with its own current, incident-scoped authority
    (Decision kind restoration). Factory Version: Suspended → Active.
  end note
  classDef control fill:#e4e9ec,stroke:#4a5d68,color:#171a18
  classDef execution fill:#f5e6d0,stroke:#9a4f1c,color:#171a18
  classDef trust fill:#dcefe4,stroke:#1a654b,color:#171a18
  classDef human fill:#e4e9ec,stroke:#b3261e,stroke-width:3px,color:#171a18
  classDef learning fill:#e9e2f4,stroke:#5c3f8f,color:#171a18
  class CLARIFY,CONTAIN human
  class OBSERVE,ISOLATE execution
  class RESTORE human
  class CORRECT trust
  class PREVENT,MEASURE learning
  class RESOLVED trust
